Interpretation: 0x6794 sets actor render byte 0x1d and invisible flag 0x10 only for living spawned non-S ring-0x2a actors after the 0x6a13 expiry roll. The actor compositor reads render byte from the sprite layer and uses bank 0x100, so the visible tile is 0x11d. 0x68ae writes 0x1e for S sleepers (tile 0x11e) after the ring pass; D actors are skipped. P and posted G actors retain 0x1d through sleep-scene mount and redraw. OUTSUBS 0x086d writes the class standing tile during each live apparition wake, before the viewport XOR; this overwrites the outline presentation while the equipped ring remains. Status rows are drawn separately; no Camp interaction command runs during sleep.
